Well, I've just gotten NetHack to compile under Borland TC++ 1.0.  The problem
is, it hangs my system, or, if I'm running QEMM 386, it brings up the 
imfamous (C)ontinue, (T)erminate, or (R)eboot.  I brought Nethack up under 
TD386, and during the loading process, it generates an "Exception 13, Error
code 0" in the C startup code.  I checked the registers, and sure enough,
DI is FFFF on a stosw instruction.  I think a data segment, perhaps the
monster table, is greater than 64K, and the compiler and linker are not
properly handling it.  I haven't tried splitting the monster database, but
anyone who's trying to compile it might want to try this.  Also, be sure to
remove the "-k-" switch from the CFLAGS macro in the makefile.  Has anyone
gotten it to run yet?

Alex


